{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  Stockists — sourced from find.non.world.

  The design shipped twelve hand-written venues. The real feed is
  find.non.world/api/stockists: ~2,200 currently-stocking venues across AU, US
  and UK, rebuilt off the Monday accounts pipeline.

  That endpoint is already the public, sanitised surface — the middleware in
  the maps project locks every host except map.non.world down to it, and the
  payload carries only venue-public fields (name, coords, suburb, region, and a
  neutral Google category). No churn state, no ROS, no rep, no order dates.
  CORS is open specifically so it can be embedded on the marketing site, so the
  theme calls it directly from the browser; nothing proxies and no key is
  needed.

  Curated blocks still exist and render above the live list as a featured
  shortlist — use them for the rooms worth naming, not for coverage.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign endpoint = section.settings.endpoint | default: 'https://find.non.world/api/stockists'
  assign find_url = section.settings.find_url | default: 'https://find.non.world'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The design opens with a statement and a live count, then closes with two
  offers: become a stockist, or skip the trip and buy direct. The port had the
  tool and nothing around it — the page answered "where" and never "what if
  the answer is nowhere near me".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign creds = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'credential' -%}
{%- if creds.size > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The design's credential strip, same component as About's. Blocks rather than
    a fixed string so each page carries its own facts — Stockists leads with the
    venue count, NONHQ with opening hours.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="non-creds">
    {%- for b in creds -%}
      <span class="non-creds__item" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>{{ b.settings.text }}</span>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="non-stock-hero">
  <div>
    <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow" data-non-hero-count>{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</div>
    <h1 class="non-stock-hero__title">{{ section.settings.hero_heading }}</h1>
  </div>
  {%- if section.settings.hero_blurb != blank -%}
    <p class="non-stock-hero__lead">{{ section.settings.hero_blurb }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

<div
  class="non-section"
  data-non-stockists
  data-endpoint="{{ endpoint }}"
  data-default-region="{{ section.settings.default_region }}"
  data-list-limit="{{ section.settings.list_limit }}">
  {%- comment -%}
    THE PANEL. design-reference puts the search, the filters, the results and
    the "see all" card in ONE left column with the map beside it — the tool is a
    single instrument you work top to bottom while the map answers alongside.

    The build had the search and filters full width ABOVE, the list and map in a
    separate row below, and the credentials wedged into the top of the list
    column. That is why the page read nothing like the design despite having
    almost every piece: the parts were all present and none of them were where
    the design puts them.

    Also gone: the region filter row. The design has one filter axis, Type. Two
    rows of chips in a narrow column reads as a database query form, and region
    is already implicit in a suburb search.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="non-stockists">
    <div class="non-stockists__list">
      <form class="non-somm non-stock-search" data-non-venue-search>
        <div class="non-somm__bar">
          <span class="non-somm__caret" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="venue-q-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.search_label }}</label>
          <input
            id="venue-q-{{ section.id }}"
            class="non-somm__input"
            type="search"
            autocomplete="off"
            data-non-venue-query
            placeholder="{{ section.settings.search_placeholder | escape }}">
          <button type="submit" class="non-somm__submit">{{ section.settings.search_cta }}</button>
        </div>
      </form>

      <div class="non-stock-filters">
        <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.filter_label }}</span>
        <div class="non-filters" role="group" aria-label="{{ section.settings.filter_label | escape }}">
          <button type="button" class="non-filter" data-non-venue-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">{{ section.settings.filter_all }}</button>
          <button type="button" class="non-filter" data-non-venue-filter="restaurant" aria-pressed="false">{{ section.settings.filter_restaurant }}</button>
          <button type="button" class="non-filter" data-non-venue-filter="bar" aria-pressed="false">{{ section.settings.filter_bar }}</button>
          <button type="button" class="non-filter" data-non-venue-filter="retail" aria-pressed="false">{{ section.settings.filter_retail }}</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The featured venues ("On the list at") used to sit HERE, at the top of
        the results column, which put four Michelin names between the customer
        and the search results they came for. The design runs them as a row of
        cards BELOW the whole panel — a credential, not a filter step. Moved
        there; see after the panel closes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-stock-listhead">
        <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow" data-non-venue-list-heading>{{ section.settings.results_label }}</div>
        {%- if section.settings.sort_note != blank -%}
          <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow non-stock-sort" data-non-venue-sort hidden>
            {{ section.settings.sort_note }}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div data-non-venues>
        <p class="non-note" style="padding:20px 0">Loading stockists…</p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The empty state. The design answers "nothing near me" with two routes out
        rather than a dead end, so both are here and both are editable. Hidden
        until stockists.js knows the result set is empty — it toggles this rather
        than writing a single line of text, which is all it used to do.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.empty_heading != blank -%}
        <div class="non-stock-empty" data-non-venue-empty hidden>
          <div class="non-stock-empty__title">{{ section.settings.empty_heading }}</div>
          {%- if section.settings.empty_body != blank -%}
            <p class="non-stock-empty__body">{{ section.settings.empty_body }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="non-stock-empty__acts">
            {%- if section.settings.empty_cta != blank -%}
              <a class="non-btn non-btn--ghost" href="{{ section.settings.find_url | default: '#' }}">
                {{ section.settings.empty_cta }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if section.settings.ship_cta != blank -%}
              <a class="non-btn" href="{{ section.settings.ship_url | default: '/collections/all' }}">
                {{ section.settings.ship_cta }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <button
        type="button"
        class="non-btn non-btn--ghost"
        data-non-venue-more
        style="margin-top:18px"
        hidden>
        Show more
      </button>

      <p class="non-error" data-non-venue-error hidden></p>

      {%- comment -%}
        The design closes the results column with a card pointing at the full
        directory — the honest admission that this page is a preview of 1,400+
        venues, not the whole list. It was missing entirely.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.all_heading != blank -%}
        <a class="non-stock-all" href="{{ section.settings.all_url | default: 'https://find.non.world' }}">
          <span class="non-stock-all__copy">
            <span class="non-stock-all__title">{{ section.settings.all_heading }}</span>
            <span class="non-stock-all__body">{{ section.settings.all_body }}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="non-mono non-stock-all__go">{{ section.settings.all_cta }} &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Map, then "Can't find it nearby?" directly beneath it — as the design has
      them, and back here after a detour. I briefly moved nominate into a
      closing band because the map column overhung the results column and left
      dead space beside it. Wrong fix: the overhang is a HEIGHT problem, solved
      by giving the map a bounded height so the two columns end together, not by
      relocating a block the design deliberately puts under the map.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="non-stockists__aside">
      {%- if section.settings.show_map -%}
        <div class="non-map" data-non-map></div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.nominate_heading != blank -%}
        <div class="non-stock-nominate">
          {%- if section.settings.nominate_label != blank -%}
            <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.nominate_label }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="non-stock-nominate__title">{{ section.settings.nominate_heading }}</div>
          {%- if section.settings.nominate_body != blank -%}
            <p class="non-stock-nominate__body">{{ section.settings.nominate_body }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.nominate_cta != blank -%}
            <a class="non-btn" href="{{ section.settings.nominate_url | default: '/pages/trade' }}">
              {{ section.settings.nominate_cta }}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    ONE closing band: the credentials and "Can't find it nearby?" side by side.

    Nominate used to hang off the bottom of the map column. The map column is
    taller than the results column, so it ran on past where the list ended and
    left a large empty rectangle to its left — a lot of dead page for one short
    paragraph. Pairing it with the credential row fills that space and makes
    both read as the page's close rather than two loose offcuts.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign venues = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'venue' -%}
  {%- if venues.size > 0 or section.settings.nominate_heading != blank -%}
    <div class="non-stock-close">
      {%- if venues.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="non-stock-listat">
          <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.featured_heading }}</div>
          <div class="non-stock-listat__row">
            {%- for block in venues -%}
              <div class="non-stock-listat__card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <div class="non-stock-listat__name">{{ block.settings.name }}</div>
                <div class="non-stock-listat__where">{{ block.settings.address }}</div>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    No closing pair here any more.

    Every page now ends with the footer group's closers, in one place, with the
    two cards chosen for the page you are on — this page gets "Got a bottle?"
    and NONHQ. This section used to render its own pair, which meant two pairs
    stacked on the stockists page and a different shape from every other page.
    The trade_* and direct_* settings are kept in the schema so the theme
    editor does not reject the template for referencing them.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  <p class="non-note" style="margin-top:28px">
    {{ section.settings.find_prompt }}
    <a href="{{ find_url }}" style="text-decoration:underline">
      {{ section.settings.find_label }}
    </a>
  </p>
</div>

{%- if section.settings.show_map -%}
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
    integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
    crossorigin="">
  <script
    src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
    integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
    crossorigin=""
    defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
<script src="{{ 'stockists.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

